================================================================================
Module Attribution Header Convention
================================================================================

Each module that ports or vendors upstream code includes a header block
(2–4 lines) documenting the upstream source, version/revision, license, and
any porting decisions. Example:

    // Ported from material_3_expressive v1.0.8 (MIT, © 2026 Paa Developments)
    // Upstream: https://github.com/paadevelopments/material_3_expressive
    // No license changes; shape semantics preserved from Dart port.

This convention is used by later design-system phases and plugin revisions
to maintain clear lineage tracking across vendored code.
